WEBVTT

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.270
Also, one can of cocoa extract, please.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.680
Very good, sir.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.850
Playing Lord of Crime?

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:29.150
Yes. My boy apparently injured
one of the other lads.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.650
I also hear that there are those aiming
to be Robin Hood figures out there.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:37.740
But this Lord of Crime is just someone
trying to justify the use of violence.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.710
I wish the children would start emulating
this young MP, instead.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.290
MP?

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:15.070
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.820
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:22.950
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.000
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.420
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.800
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.180
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.760
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.350
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:50.480
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.110
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.240
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.330
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:05.660
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.120
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.000
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.800
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.680
"The White Knight of London
Act 1"
--Young upstart!
--Who do you think you are?!

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.390
"The White Knight of London
Act 1"
Quiet! Order, please!

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.560
Please continue your remarks,

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.770
Mr Whiteley.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:38.400
Oi, he's coming out!

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.780
Mr Whiteley, this is the third time you
have proposed your election reform bill!

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.700
Assuming your bill passes
the House of Commons,

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.630
it seems evident that it will be
defeated in the House of Lords!

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:56.380
I knew that there would be such opposition
before even proposing the bill.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.340
However, for the sake of
the nation's development,

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:04.600
the right to vote must be extended
to all citizens in the working class.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:05.930
To that end,

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.810
I will see to it that it is enacted
during this session, no matter what!

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:13.360
There is much opposition within
the House of Commons, as well!

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.900
Do you have some secret strategy
to wear down the House of Lords?

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.570
I will convince them somehow.
You can count on that!

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:22.410
Please, step inside.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.450
Right. Thank you.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.370
What is that smell?

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.830
It couldn't be...!

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:32.750
It's a bomb!

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:36.000
Get away from the carriage
at once! Quickly!

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.530
Tell me, who the blazes hired you?!

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.870
Whatever do you mean?

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.580
Mr Whiteley, are you all right?!

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.490
Yes. But never mind me, search this man.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:12.580
This man? But why?

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:17.040
I have many occasions
to speak before large crowds,

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.920
and whenever I look into
each one of their faces,

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.470
I can tell in an instant
what they are thinking about.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:28.390
Faces brimming with expectations,
pinning their hopes on me.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:32.350
Faces of those who are doubtful
and sceptical of me.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:37.020
And faces such as his,
who wish death upon me.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.570
Th-There are fuses in his bag!

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.820
Nicely done, Mr Whiteley.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.660
Everyone, listen to me!

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:50.240
I will never back down
to this kind of violence!

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.250
I promise you, I will get my
election reform bill passed!

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.670
Because...

00:04:55.670 --> 00:05:01.210
...the achievement of equality
is my mission, and my dream!

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:03.470
Whiteley!

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.260
Adam Whiteley!

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:08.350
You are our delegate!

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:15.980
"Assassination attempt on Whiteley MP.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.610
Some say he staged it himself
to gain publicity.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:23.940
Is the white knight a swindler
peddling 'equality'?"

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:29.450
As far as I know, there is nothing shady
about what Mr Whiteley says.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.240
He is an MP of unquestionable integrity.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:38.080
How far does he intend to carry on
under the banner of equality?

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.880
What do you think, William?

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:45.590
The bomber was likely a mobster,
hired by the House of Lords.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.090
If the connection to
the House of Lords is made,

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:51.260
and he becomes the standard bearer
for a popular revolution,

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:53.350
then election reform

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:57.730
and the prime minister's post
will be his for the taking.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.690
However, on the other hand,

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:03.480
political and social unrest
within the country will increase,

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:10.120
and the lives of many people could easily
be lost to violence and mayhem.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:13.990
Whether or not that is
the situation he is hoping for...

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.750
...is something I would like
to test him about.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:21.460
"Equality," eh? Any politician who
carries on about anything so lofty

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.170
is not on the level.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:28.430
No, we cannot say that
for sure yet, Moran.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.260
Depending on how Whiteley acts,

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:37.230
this country might be led to equality
without any need of help from us.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.820
Oi, it's time for your supper--

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:54.700
B-Blimey!

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:57.290
Somebody call a doctor!

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:02.210
The bomber who came after me is dead?

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.880
Yes. He was stabbed through
the throat with a pen,

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.090
and the guard discovered him
after he had died from loss of blood.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.800
The Criminal Investigation Department

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.260
is investigating it from both
the suicide and homicide angles.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:17.060
What is happening here?

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:22.980
I am terribly sorry that such a mishap
occurred in my own station, Mr Whiteley.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.190
It's hard to believe that
a mobster in it for the money

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:29.570
would kill himself out of loyalty
to the House of Lords.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:31.740
If it was a homicide...

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:36.830
...then the only conclusion is that
there is a collaborator within the Yard.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.830
Chief Inspector Paterson, it is going
to be much more difficult now

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:43.500
to determine who hired our bomber,

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.210
and though it gives me pause to ask,

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:52.090
would you allow me to choose those
conducting the investigation henceforth?

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:54.340
You wish to select the personnel?

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.640
Yes.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:00.430
Allow me to handle this.
I have a good eye for judging people.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.820
This article won't do.
We are a high-class--

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.410
Good morning, Mr President.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.620
--Good morning, sir.
--Good morning.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.040
--Good morning...
--Good morning.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:27.000
Good morning, Mr Milverton.
Did you speak with the House of Lords?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.300
Yes.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.340
If only they had asked me sooner.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:36.350
Sending threats via mobsters
and attempted assassinations...

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:38.760
If they had killed Whiteley
at that moment,

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:43.770
he would have been the hero who died
a martyr for the great cause of equality.

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:49.480
What an utter pack of fools.
There's no call for such a sloppy move.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:53.990
I have been hired by the House of Lords
to dispose of Whiteley.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:58.410
I will carry out my task in my own way.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.450
Then, once again...

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.120
Yes.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:05.420
I will smear this good man Whiteley,

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:09.000
and drag him down from
his righteous knight's spot.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:15.430
I'm going to watch his dramatic downfall
from the best seats in the house.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.640
Albert,

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:27.150
everything is ready.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:31.230
I would like to put Mr Whiteley
to the test tomorrow.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.320
Mm-hmm.

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:38.410
I also have what you
requested ready to go.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.490
Thank you very much, Brother.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:47.830
I only hope that he, like us,

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:52.420
is someone who can move forward
despite the accompanying pain.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.890
Maggie, where is the morning edition?

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.890
Oh... Well, now...

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.980
Then the front page is once again
full of denigration toward me.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:13.230
It doesn't bother me one bit.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:14.990
Would you mind bringing it here?

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:19.160
All right, but don't say
I didn't warn you.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:22.030
Good morning, Mr Whiteley.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:25.410
Inspector Robinson, Inspector Sturridge.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:29.580
Come, sit down, both of you,
and join me for breakfast.

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:35.210
You all eat breakfast together,
I see. Very cosy, I must say.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:40.720
It's always like this here. Inspectors,
you should hurry and get used to it.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:44.350
Also, Maggie's pies are truly delicious.

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:47.270
Well, I look forward to trying one.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:49.900
Good morning, Adam.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:55.030
And, er... Mr Robinson and Mr Sturridge.
Good morning to you, too, Marcus.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:11:01.620
Good morning, Sam. We are
joining you for breakfast today.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.330
Where's Maggie?

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:06.120
She must be making a fuss about
snipping out the defamation toward me

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.790
in this morning's newspaper.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:13.210
Maggie is just worried about you, Brother.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:16.420
That goes for all of the threatening
letters that arrive every day.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:20.720
And just yesterday, there was an attempt
on your life, wasn't there?

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:24.720
Maggie isn't the only one, either. I...

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:27.390
Sam...

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:29.690
I understand your concerns.

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:33.900
However, I'm not the sort of man
who allows his will to be shaped...

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:36.650
...or who backs down to cowards
who level threats.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.990
No, but...

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:42.160
Once my bill passes, and things change,

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:48.250
I know a world of equality will be coming,
where you will be free of this toil.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.910
Brother, I--

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:55.040
Yes, quite right! Your brother
is going to change the world!

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:58.760
That is why we have taken on
the responsibility to protect him.

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.510
Although things have proved challenging,

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:03.090
our investigation into these
threatening letters is proceeding,

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:05.800
so please, try not to worry.

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:14.480
Sam, are you sure you won't be
coming to the ceremony today?

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:20.240
I'm sorry, no. Do come back safely,
Brother. Take care.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:23.700
Right. Off I go, then.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:33.920
The inspectors are with him.
I'm sure he'll be fine.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:45.930
The park we worked so hard
to bring about is nearly finished.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:50.430
Sir, you will be making
your remarks after the mayor.

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:55.020
Also, all of the guests that you invited

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:58.230
will be allowed into the park once
the ceremony is concluded.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:00.190
Very good.

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.740
Thank you.

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.780
I can hardly wait.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:10.200
Wh-What the...? What the devil
is going on here?!

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.790
This is not at all what was planned.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:18.540
What are all the MPs who
opposed his bill doing here?

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:22.880
Now even the mayor will take
the view of all those MPs,

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:28.350
and this whole ceremony will turn into
a condemnation of Mr Whiteley!

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:33.600
Ladies and gentlemen of the city,
good day. I am Mayor Dempster.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:37.440
It brings me great pleasure
to be able to stand here today

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:41.440
to announce the completion of this park.

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:47.990
Looking back, the path we took to complete
this park was not an easy one.

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:49.530
There were issues of public safety,

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.200
and issues of pollution,

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:54.040
but the greatest issue we faced...

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:58.580
...was none other than Adam Whiteley MP,
right over there!

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:05.380
After all, he revoked the plans for
this park after they had been approved!

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:07.220
Whiteley did that?

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:09.470
Is this true?

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:18.020
Moreover, he forced his own newly
designed plans for the park on us!

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.860
As a result,

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:22.480
the park far exceeded its original budget,

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:28.450
and for a time, the construction of
the park itself nearly came to a halt!

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.820
--That can't be true.
--But we were undaunted by
the obstacles he placed before us,

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:34.580
and tenaciously proceeded
to move the project forward.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:39.370
For you see, we wished for this
to become a beautiful park!

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:45.550
The greatest source of influence in
creating this park is not Mr Whiteley;

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:52.390
it is none other than these members
of parliament over here!

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:57.810
Now, let us ask Mr Spencer to
speak to us on behalf of the group.

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.850
Ladies and gentlemen of the city,

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:06.240
it pains me to have to speak about
this on a day as glorious as this one,

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:09.780
but I would like to take this
opportunity to say a few words.

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:15.160
Mr Whiteley, as much as with this park,
as with his election reform bill,

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:17.790
has been every bit a dictator!

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:21.960
Despite not reaching a consensus
in the House of Commons,

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.380
he took it upon himself
to submit his bill,

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.920
and the reformation dialogue
that had been proceeding

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.050
behind closed doors with
the House of Lords

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:33.930
has been derailed, thanks to
Mr Whiteley's runaway actions!

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:37.680
In other words, the one standing
in the way of any reform...

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:41.440
...is none other than Mr Whiteley himself!

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:46.190
<i>He's </i>standing in the way? That's absurd!

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:48.900
Regular negotiations
with the House of Lords

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.990
would take 30 years to pass any reforms!

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:56.990
That is why he is risking
his life to go it alone!

00:15:56.990 --> 00:16:00.910
Ladies and gentlemen, I ask you
to please decide for yourselves

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:05.090
who it is that is truly acting in
the best interests of the people,

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:07.800
and not give ear to only
the things you wish to hear!

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:10.380
Thank you for your attention!

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:14.180
Mr Spencer, thank you very much.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:16.100
Is what he just said true?

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.640
I'm not sure.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:21.270
Let's hear what Whiteley has to say.

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:25.730
And now, we will hear some
remarks from Mr Whiteley.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:49.000
What you just heard from the mayor
and Mr Spencer concerning this park...

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.590
...is all true.

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:52.760
--Huh?!
--That's madness!

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:54.930
--What?!
--Are you serious?!

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:56.180
You aren't denying it?!

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.310
We believed in you!

00:16:58.310 --> 00:17:02.600
It is true that my own ego
made me interpose my own plans.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:06.150
Also, I was aware that both houses
were at work behind the scenes

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.150
making efforts toward
bringing about reforms.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:13.860
However, I nonetheless
proceeded to propose my bill.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.110
Lastly, I would like to apologise

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:22.410
that the completion of this park
was greatly delayed on my account.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.790
That is all I have to say.

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:26.330
Huh? That's all?!

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:28.880
That doesn't explain a thing!

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:32.840
He must have something shady going on
preventing him from saying more.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:37.090
My word, what a disappointment.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.350
Sir!

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:46.980
Why didn't you refute them?!

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:48.480
Refute them?

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:53.570
If you would have outlined your
intentions in designing this park--

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:57.280
how you wanted to do more
than just create a "regular park,"

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:01.410
I'm sure everyone here would
have understood! Moreover...

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:06.670
...I am so frustrated that
your honour has been tarnished!

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.710
My honour?

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:17.130
That doesn't matter. Forget about that,
and look there, Marcus.

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:22.140
It appears that my guests have arrived.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:26.190
Brilliant!

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:29.770
This park really is
all completely one level!

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:32.230
We'll be safe playing here!

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:36.200
Hey, I'll race you to that tree!

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:38.820
Children, don't do anything reckless!

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:41.030
What the...?

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:43.370
This is what I wanted to see.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:46.710
The smiles on those children's faces
are everything.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:50.710
I have accomplished my goal.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:52.500
Sir...

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:09.770
Aren't you... Lord Moriarty?

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:13.690
Good day, Mr Whiteley.
Please forgive my abruptness,

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:16.490
but I would like to have
a brief word with you alone.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:18.240
Hmm?

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.280
Lord Moriarty,

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:28.500
why would you, a member of the
House of Lords, wish to speak with me?

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:33.590
As it happens, I have a request
that only you can fulfil.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.210
What is this?

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:39.380
What you need right now--

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:44.260
irrefutable proof of the link between
the House of Lords and the mobsters.

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:46.930
As long as you have that,

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.390
you will be able to conduct backroom
dealings with the House of Lords.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:53.360
Why would you give me
something that puts yourself

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.820
in such a precarious position?

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:57.070
You may find this hard to believe,

00:19:57.070 --> 00:20:02.070
but I, too, have grown entirely fed up
with how the House of Lords operates.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.570
Besides,

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:06.200
I am sure that you will not
use this evidence of injustice

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:10.250
to further your own honour.

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:14.840
Once I made that determination,
I decided to entrust that to you.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:16.210
Lord Moriarty...

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:20.550
Hmph, as long as you
remain who you now are,

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:25.300
I will stand with you. That is all.

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:38.360
He is quite a pleasant man, William.

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:41.240
Thanks to the ceremony
that you orchestrated,

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:45.030
we were able to make certain
of Mr Whiteley's humanity.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:49.490
Yes. But the power we have given him...

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:52.710
...may yet prove to force
some difficult choices,

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:57.210
both for him, as well as for us.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.880
Still...

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:02.510
if we had done nothing,
then he, without this power,

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:06.390
was destined to be eliminated
eventually in any case.

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:11.390
There is always a price to be paid
to achieve any objective.

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:17.110
All the more true when it comes to the
colossal goal of transforming this nation.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:24.360
Yes, Brother.

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:31.250
Let's go.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:45.090
W-Wait! I did as you said...

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:48.220
...and killed the criminal
who went after Whiteley...!

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:50.890
S-Spare me--

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.690
Good. Mr Milverton instructed us

00:21:57.690 --> 00:22:01.650
to make sure that this
officer's body would be found.

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:04.030
Go dump him somewhere suitable.

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:07.320
Then our next target...

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:12.040
...is Sam Whiteley--

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:14.450
the MP's brother.

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:23.710
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:31.930
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:42.520
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:45.900
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:49.910
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:53.290
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:22:53.290 --> 00:23:00.710
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:09.300
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:17.100
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:23.360
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:26.150
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:31.820
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:23:31.820 --> 00:23:38.500
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>

00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:52.050
Next time on <i>Moriarty The Patriot</i>:
"The White Knight of London Act 2."
